From 63af364f0498580a3f373b4616aa3a5479f33ab7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 14:43:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v2.9.8: native Backup & Restore page; Complete-restore one
 click from the landing page

Owner items after the v2.9.7 metal pass confirmed both restore modes:

1. Reaper_Backup.asp - a reaper-native page owns every backup/restore
   surface: full .rbk backup/restore, Reaper settings JSON export/import,
   stock router settings .CFG save/restore (remove-password + ASUS-DDNS
   transfer flags kept), JFFS partition backup/restore (jffs2_on-gated,
   stock jffsupload.cgi file2 contract), and factory default reset
   (apply.cgi Restore / restore_erase) - with the themed confirm modal,
   one-shot-guarded liveness polling after reboot-class actions, and the
   changed-LAN-IP exit message when the box never answers again.
2. The stock Administration > Restore/Save/Upload page is retired from the
   menu (menuTrees/menuTree.js repointed, stock file kept on disk as the
   fallback) and SUP-redirected to the native page; the v2.7.2 injected
   card (mode 4, REAPER_BKCARD_JS + Reaper_BackupCard.asp fragment) is
   absorbed by the native page and deleted.
3. Pending-restore banner on reaper_shell.asp (above every framed page) and
   Main_ReaperDash.asp (the post-login landing page): after a full-backup
   restore reboots the box, the Reaper half is one visible click anywhere -
   the banner carries the Complete restore button and reports the counts
   in place. Hidden and cost-free when nothing is pending.

i18n: RBKP_19..RBKP_26 appended to all 25 dicts (translated), lockstep
6792. verify_markers + reaper_langcheck OUR updated in lean + engine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
