+     fallback) and absorbs the injected Reaper_BackupCard.asp fragment, which is
+     retired with it. Owns every backup/restore surface:
+       - full .rbk backup/restore (reaper_restore.cgi / the .rbk download)
+       - Reaper settings JSON export/import (reaper_cfg.cgi)
+       - stock router settings .CFG save/restore (Settings_*.CFG / upload.cgi)
+       - JFFS partition backup/restore (backup_jffs_*.tar / jffsupload.cgi,
+         part name "file2", jffs2_on-gated)
+       - factory default reset (apply.cgi action_mode=Restore / restore_erase)
+     The pending-restore banner also lives in reaper_shell.asp and
+     Main_ReaperDash.asp so "Complete restore" is one click from the landing
+     page after the post-restore reboot; this page keeps its own copy because
+     it is where the restore started. -->
+<!DOCTYPE html>
